# <type>(<scope>): <short description>
# 
# <body>
# 
# <footer>

# Commit format follows Conventional Commits 1.0
# - Type must be one of the types listed below
# - <body> and <footer> are optional
# - all lowercase short description
# - Lists of summaries for complex descriptions
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COMMIT TYPES:
#   feat     : A new feature or significant added functionality
#   fix      : A bug patch or correction
#   docs     : Documentation changes only (e.g., README updates)
#   style    : Code formatting, missing semi-colons, white-space changes
#   refactor : Code restructuring that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf     : Code changes that specifically improve performance
#   test     : Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
#   build    : Changes affecting the build system or external dependencies
#   ci       : Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
#   chore    : Routine maintenance tasks or auxiliary tools
#   revert   : Reverting a previous commit
#
# RULES:
#   - Append a '!' after the type/scope for BREAKING CHANGES.
#   - Write the short description in the imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period.
#   - Keep the first line under 72 characters.
#   - Separate the subject line from the body with a blank line.
# 
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
